 continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4y)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2xz) \\\\  & =-2x+4+2x \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid sphere of radius $1$ enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}4\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & =4{∭}_{R}\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\text{Volume}(R) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}\\pi \\cdot {1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535868 true] [17592186371398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371399 13194139535868 true] [17592186371398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371400 13194139535868 true] [17592186371398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371401 13194139535868 true] [17592186371398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371402 13194139535868 true] [17592186371398 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371403 13194139535868 true] [17592186371398 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535868 true] [17592186371398 1041 "selection" 13194139535868 true] [17592186371398 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371401 13194139535868 true] [17592186371398 1110 #uuid "bf337090-c8b2-5aea-bf56-8bd215441650" 13194139535868 true] [17592186371399 1034 "12\\pi " 13194139535868 true] [17592186371399 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535868 true] [17592186371399 1111 #uuid "e638f438-e1e3-56c9-bd6b-174ba4f5d383" 13194139535868 true] [17592186371400 1034 "\\frac{32\\pi }{3}" 13194139535868 true] [17592186371400 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535868 true] [17592186371400 1111 #uuid "0d52b91e-ccf6-58f2-b6b6-81c579b27d80" 13194139535868 true] [17592186371401 1034 "\\frac{16\\pi }{3}" 13194139535868 true] [17592186371401 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535868 true] [17592186371401 1111 #uuid "576b65e8-29bb-5e90-9496-d6481c6e4fac" 13194139535868