or field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2x+2+0 \\\\  & =2x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}(2x+2)\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(2x+2)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{2}\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{3}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[{x}^{2}+2x]_{x=0}^{x=1}\\cdot (2-1)\\cdot (3-1) \\\\  & =({1}^{2}+2(1)-0)\\cdot 1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535868 true] [17592186371447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371448 13194139535868 true] [17592186371447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371449 13194139535868 true] [17592186371447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371450 13194139535868 true] [17592186371447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371451 13194139535868 true] [17592186371447 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371452 13194139535868 true] [17592186371447 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535868 true] [17592186371447 1041 "selection" 13194139535868 true] [17592186371447 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371451 13194139535868 true] [17592186371447 1110 #uuid "42f89423-06ad-5708-9940-540ddda32b60" 13194139535868 true] [17592186371448 1034 "3" 13194139535868 true] [17592186371448 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535868 true] [17592186371448 1111 #uuid "c4ce8af8-1cab-53b7-b4be-fbaab6ecc90b" 13194139535868 true] [17592186371449 1034 "8" 13194139535868 true] [17592186371449 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535868 true] [17592186371449 1111 #uuid "8908ab80-4a54-5c16-bebf-26d72f20ef7a" 13194139535868 true] [17592186371450 1034 "2" 13194139535868 true